# CLI

Reference for the `wyrd` binary. It has four command groups: `auth`, `eval`,
`principal`, and `gateway`. The binary is built from the repo — see [Get started](/get-started/).

Every server-facing command reads `--server` from `WYRD_SERVER_URL` when the flag
is omitted. No command takes a secret as an argument: server-facing commands
read their credential from the ambient chain (`WYRD_ACCESS_TOKEN`, workload
identity, `WYRD_API_KEY`, or `~/.config/wyrd/credentials.toml`), so it never
lands in shell history or the process table.

## wyrd auth

Authenticate with a Wyrd server and manage credentials.

### auth login

Initiate an OIDC login flow and exchange the callback code for a Wyrd access
token. Prints a URL to open in your browser.

```bash
wyrd auth login --server https://acme.wyrd.cloud --issuer https://id.acme.com
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Flag', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Required' },
    { header: 'Env' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['--server', 'yes', 'WYRD_SERVER_URL', 'Wyrd server base URL.'],
    ['--issuer', 'yes', '—', 'Trusted OIDC issuer URL registered with this tenant.']
  ]}
/>

### auth refresh

Rotate a human session's Wyrd refresh token and print the new access and
refresh tokens. Only a `User` principal holds one; a machine renews by
re-exchanging its API key instead. The refresh token is read only from
`WYRD_REFRESH_TOKEN`.

```bash
WYRD_REFRESH_TOKEN="$TOKEN" wyrd auth refresh --server https://acme.wyrd.cloud
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Flag', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Required' },
    { header: 'Env' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['--server', 'yes', 'WYRD_SERVER_URL', 'Wyrd server base URL.']
  ]}
/>

### auth issue-key

Issue an API key bound to a card ref (`POST /auth/issue-key`). Requires an admin
credential in the ambient chain.

```bash
wyrd auth issue-key \
  --kind service --name checkout --version 1.0.0 --space prod \
  --server https://acme.wyrd.cloud
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Flag', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Required' },
    { header: 'Env' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['--kind', 'yes', '—', 'Card kind the key is bound to (e.g. service, agent).'],
    ['--name', 'yes', '—', 'Card name.'],
    ['--version', 'yes', '—', 'Card version (e.g. 1.0.0).'],
    ['--space', 'yes', '—', 'Card space.'],
    ['--label', 'no', '—', 'Label stored with the key row.'],
    ['--expires-in-seconds', 'no', '—', 'TTL override in seconds.'],
    ['--server', 'yes', 'WYRD_SERVER_URL', 'Wyrd server base URL.']
  ]}
/>

## wyrd eval run

Score pre-collected observations locally against an Eval-backed Verifier card
(`kind: Verifier` with `implementation.kind: eval`). The command reads a local
card file and a JSONL of records; it does not contact a server.

```bash
wyrd eval run --eval ./verifier.yaml --records ./observations.jsonl \
  --subject support/Agent/triage@1.0.0
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Flag', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Default' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['--eval', '(required)', 'Eval-backed Verifier card filesystem path (JSON or YAML).'],
    ['--records', '(required)', 'JSONL of pre-collected EvalRecordObservation rows.'],
    ['--subject', '(required)', 'CardRef of the Card that emitted the records.'],
    ['--judge-mock', 'false', 'Deterministic judge — all LLM judge tasks return passed: true. Required if the spec has LLM judges and no provider is configured.'],
    ['--baseline', '—', 'Baseline EvalResults JSON for comparison.'],
    ['--out', '—', 'Directory for local output artifacts (env WYRD_EVAL_OUT).'],
    ['--fail-on-gate', 'true', 'Exit non-zero when the local pass gate fails.']
  ]}
/>

## wyrd principal revoke

Suspend a principal so it can mint no new token; tokens it already holds lapse
within five minutes. Requires an admin credential in the ambient chain. The
principal ID is positional; `--kind` is required because IDs are unique only
within a kind.

```bash
wyrd principal revoke 3f9a...uuid --kind service --reason "key leaked" \
  --server https://acme.wyrd.cloud
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Argument', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Required' },
    { header: 'Env' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['<id>', 'yes', '—', 'Principal ID (UUID) to revoke.'],
    ['--kind', 'yes', '—', 'Principal kind: user, service, or agent.'],
    ['--reason', 'yes', '—', 'Audit reason for the revocation.'],
    ['--server', 'yes', 'WYRD_SERVER_URL', 'Wyrd server base URL.']
  ]}
/>

## wyrd gateway

Administer tenant gateway resources. Every verb prints the server's JSON
response on stdout (deletes print nothing) and failures print the originating
problem on stderr. See [Administer the gateway](/how-to/administer-the-gateway/)
for lifecycle rules.

```bash
wyrd gateway credential put --file credential.json
WYRD_ACCESS_TOKEN=... wyrd gateway deployment list --server https://acme.wyrd.cloud
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Command', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['credential put --file <path>', 'Create or rotate the credential named in the document.'],
    ['credential get <name> | list', 'Read redacted credentials.'],
    ['credential revoke <name>', 'Terminally revoke a credential.'],
    ['credential delete <name>', 'Delete an unreferenced credential; absent names succeed.'],
    ['deployment put --file <path> | get <name> | list | delete <name>', 'Manage provider deployments.'],
    ['fallback-policy put --file <path> | get | delete', 'Replace, read, or reset the fallback policy.'],
    ['governance-policy put --file <path> | get | delete', 'Replace, read, or reset the governance policy.'],
    ['capture-policy put --file <path> | get', 'Replace or read the capture policy.'],
    ['--server', 'Wyrd server base URL (WYRD_SERVER_URL). Credentials resolve from WYRD_ACCESS_TOKEN, WYRD_API_KEY, or client configuration; the CLI never accepts them as arguments.']
  ]}
/>

